# The web image copies the whole monorepo, so this file is load-bearing in two
# ways: it keeps the build context small, and it keeps .env out of the image.
# An image layer is not a secret store — anyone who can pull the image can read
# it, and on a public Space that is everyone.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Reinstalled inside the image. Copying the host's tree in would mix Windows
# binaries and symlinks into a Linux image, and pnpm would then have to undo it.
node_modules
**/node_modules

# Python virtualenv, same reasoning — host-specific interpreters and paths.
apps/ytmusic/.venv
**/__pycache__
*.egg-info

# Build output, rebuilt in the image.
.next
**/.next

.git
.github
docs
*.md
!README.md
